# cuts/v1.0.54/cut.env -- the pins this cut is made from.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY v1.0.54 AND NOT v1.0.53 -- READ THIS BEFORE "TIDYING" THE VERSION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1.0.53 was tagged at 8f66b632 on 2026-08-30T18:10:50Z and its preflight
# refused with FOUR failures. Every one of them is a condition ON THE TREE AT
# THAT COMMIT:
#
#   cuts/v1.0.53/cut.env           ABSENT at 8f66b632
#   cuts/v1.0.53/MUST_CONTAIN.tsv  ABSENT at 8f66b632
#   walk closure                   v1.0.52 had no rollforward row
#   gui/project.yml                MARKETING_VERSION "1.0.52", not "1.0.53"
#
# 🔴 THE TAG WAS BORN DEAD, and that is stronger than "it went stale". Fixing
# any of the four requires a NEW COMMIT, so main necessarily moves PAST the
# tag, and the tag keeps pointing at a tree that can never satisfy the gates.
# Re-running the cut against it fails identically, forever. TNM measured this
# at source rather than inferring it from the ordering.
#
# THE INVARIANT, and it is the reason this file exists before any tag:
#
#     A CUT TAG MUST BE CREATED AFTER EVERY CONDITION IT WILL BE JUDGED ON.
#
# Task #905 recorded a weaker version of this ("the tag goes stale on every
# prerequisite merge, five times in 90 minutes"). Today shows it is not a race
# that can be lost -- tagging first makes the tag unsatisfiable WITH CERTAINTY,
# because the version bump preflight demands is itself a commit and no commit
# can precede the tag cut before it.
#
# ⚠️ v1.0.53 IS NOT DELETED AND MUST NOT BE. It published nothing -- no release
# object, no bytes, no artefact -- but the ref truthfully records a tree that
# was tagged and refused. Force-repointing it would have made ONE VERSION NAME
# TWO TREES, which is the two-artefacts-one-version class this project filed
# against itself the same night. Versions are cheap; a version that names two
# trees is not. ABANDONED, recorded, not reused.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DAEMON_COMMIT -- ADVANCED DELIBERATELY, and this is the rare case where it is
# correct to move it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1.0.52 carried f1c7c57d and its header says, correctly, "do not advance this
# line" -- because that cut REBUILT NO DAEMON. This one does. hub-v0.4.69 was
# built from oa c6fc48c0 on the shipping lane and PUBLISHED to both halves:
#
#   ostler-ai/ostler-releases    ostler-assistant-aarch64-apple-darwin-v0.4.69.tar.gz
#                                10,162,166 B  sha256 e680396893fadd78...fc92a84f
#                                Developer-ID signed, notarised, ticket stapled,
#                                spctl accepted as Notarized Developer ID
#   ostler-ai/ostler-assistant   ostler-hub-app-aarch64-apple-darwin-v0.4.69.tar.gz
#                                3,697,727 B   sha256 3e030adb594c5f73...2ab2a8b8
#                                ADHOC BY DESIGN -- the cut re-signs it via
#                                embed-sparkle.sh codesign --force --deep, which
#                                would discard any earlier ticket
#
# 🔴 TWO REPOS, ONE TAG. gui/Makefile:262 DAEMON_REPO = ostler-releases serves
# the daemon; gui/Makefile:305 HUB_APP_REPO = ostler-assistant serves the hub
# app; both are fetched at $(DAEMON_RELEASE_TAG). Publishing only one half
# leaves the cut 404ing on the other, AND the hub-app fetch path is NEVER TAKEN
# on the operator's Mac, so a missing half is invisible here and fails in a
# clean room. Found by TNM before the re-pin, not after.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THIS CUT CARRIES
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ONE customer-visible fix, and the honesty about that matters more than the
# count: oa #369 = Andy's #454 from the v1.0.52 walk. He said "we agreed that
# there wouldn't be this 'Advanced' section". The Advanced surface is gone from
# Settings and its two customer-facing controls -- the daily-brief schedule and
# the iMessage message prefix -- are mounted on Preferences, so nothing is lost.
# Deleting the link alone would have re-created #877, where those controls were
# orphaned with no route to them.
#
# VERIFIED INSIDE THE SIGNED ARTEFACT, two-sided with a predicate control:
#   "Open advanced settings"      0   specimen, gone
#   "More settings"               0   specimen, gone
#   "Mark assistant texts with"   1   control, present
#   "Daily brief"                 1   control, present
#   "Assistant name"              1   control, proves the reader can see the file
#   a never-present token         0   negative control
#
# DOES NOT CARRY -- five of Andy's six v1.0.52 findings, stated so the walk is
# not a surprise. See cuts/DEFECTS_ROLLFORWARD.md rows v1052-D001..D006:
#   A1 #595/#210  Front Page dead: the store-auth shim enumerates .venv dirs and
#                 cm059-editor has none, so its producer 401s hourly and
#                 fail-closes to the settling stub. Fix merged (#1302), NOT WALKED.
#   A3 #218       the "Still getting to know you" panel: four CSS classes the
#                 renderer emits are undefined, and the <ul> class is applied to
#                 a <table>. CM044, A2 holds it.
#   A4 #482       Bursar: 2 of 5 required usage-journal producers do not exist.
#                 ANDY'S SCOPE CALL, not a defect to code around.
#   A5 #594       "Duplicate review is available on the Hub Mac only" rendered ON
#                 the Hub Mac. CM044 #262 merged; needs a wiki-image rebuild and
#                 re-pin to reach a box.
#   A6 #300/#346  dedupe: ~30 genuine over-merges (not 136 -- A2 corrected their
#                 own figure), through the SHAREABLE-id path, and the
#                 discriminator test against the shipping resolver is not run.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS CUT HAS NO WALK RECORD AT THE MOMENT IT IS MADE, AND THAT IS CORRECT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# walks/v1.0.54.tsv does not exist, so verify_walk_record.sh returns rc=2 --
# absence, correctly not conflated with badness -- PROMOTE=0, the release is a
# prerelease, and ostler.ai/install.dmg keeps resolving to its current target.
# The sequence is cut -> walk -> record -> only then promote.
#
# ⚠️ PUT THE DMG IN THE WALKED ACCOUNT'S ~/Downloads. post_walk_qa.sh looks in
# only $HOME/Downloads, $HOME/Desktop and $HOME of the ssh user it walks as, and
# on a CLEAN record the gate then REQUIRES artefact_sha256_source to read
# measured(...). A clean walk whose DMG sits elsewhere produces PROMOTE=0 for a
# reason that reads as "no walk evidence" rather than "wrong folder".

CUT_VERSION=1.0.54
DAEMON_COMMIT=c6fc48c0
CM051=8f66b632c2b8ecba74eb4147b9bd05edebae5d59
